.TH AGENT-HOOK-SESSION-START 1 "2026-10-13" "agentguard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-hook-session-start \- emit startup context for an agent session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-hook-session-start
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-hook-session-start
reads a session-start hook JSON payload from standard input, reports repository
context, warns on local environment issues such as high disk usage, and asks
Hive Memory for startup context when
.BR hm (1)
is installed and configured.
.PP
When a session is launched from
.BR $HOME ,
AgentGuard treats that as no active project instead of passing the home
directory as a project hint.
.PP
On runtimes with Hive Memory delivery tracking (Claude Code, Codex, Muse), a
start with
.B source
.BR compact ,
.BR clear ,
or
.BR resume ,
and the first start for a session key, also start a new Hive Memory context
epoch and inject startup context again; a repeated plain start does not. If
that reset fails or re-sends no memory context, the next
.BR agent-hook-prompt-submit (1)
requests it again. With less than 2 KB left under the host limit, or after
three overflows since the last compaction, clear, or resume, the start runs
untracked, as without tracking, and the reset stays pending.
.PP
Every start also removes the session's edit-churn bypass marker (see
.BR agentguard-churn-bypass (1))
from every state root, so a reused session key never inherits a
previous session's bypass.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_HIVE_MEMORY_HOOKS
Set to
.B 0
to disable Hive Memory hook integration.
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_HIVE_MEMORY_DELIVERY
Set to
.BR 0 ,
.BR false ,
.BR no ,
or
.B off
to keep every runtime on untracked Hive Memory hooks.
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_HIVE_MEMORY_CONTEXT_RESERVE
Minimum bytes of the host limit to keep free for context added after Hive
Memory (default 0). The hook otherwise reserves the context that last pushed
a response over the limit (capped at half the limit unless two overflows were
consecutive) until the next compaction, clear, or resume, or a Muse
project-change block.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Startup context was emitted or no context was available.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agent-hook-compact (1),
.BR agent-hook-prompt-submit (1),
.BR hm (1)
